# Digital Awareness: A Model for School Counselors

**Authors:** Chibbaro, Julia S., Ricks, Lacey, Lanier, Bethany

## Abstract
As the integration of technology into schools is becoming prevalent, school counselors and educators must work together to identify students who may be suffering from digital addiction. As a student advocate and leader within their schools, school counselors are in an optimal position to educate school staff, students, and community members on the signs and symptoms, dangers, and treatments of digital addiction. Early identification of digital addiction is essential for the well-being of all students.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1222989

